  "quast.ambiguityNote": "When a contig's best alignment covers more than 99 % of it, QUAST keeps that alignment (and any scoring at least 0.99 × as well) and skips the others. A circular contig that starts just past the reference's origin can therefore lose its short end piece from the genome fraction: on ARVA's synthetic genome, a chromosome identical to the reference but rotated by 1,000 of 300,000 bp gave 99.683 %.",
