  "quast.def.same": "ARVA's assembly card counts every contig; for this check ARVA leaves out the contigs shorter than {min} bp, as QUAST does, so both describe the same contigs (the '(>= 0 bp)' rows count all of them in both programs).",
  "quast.def.nx": "N50, N90, L50, L90 have the same definition in both programs: sort the contigs by length, longest first; Nx is the length of the contig at which the running total first reaches x % of the total length, and Lx is its rank (QUAST compares in floating point, ARVA in whole numbers).",
  "quast.def.gc": "GC (%): QUAST divides G + C by all bases except N, after turning the IUPAC codes M, K, R, Y, W, S, V, B, H, D into N; ARVA divides G + C by A + C + G + T. On the files QUAST accepts (A, C, G, T, N and those codes) the two give the same value.",
  "quast.def.rounding": "QUAST prints GC and N's per 100 kbp with two decimals; ARVA's value is shown with four and counts as equal when it rounds to QUAST's.",
  "quast.def.ns": "# N's per 100 kbp: QUAST turns the IUPAC codes into N before counting, so ARVA compares its count of N plus the other IUPAC codes; the 'N per 100 kb' on ARVA's assembly card counts N only.",
