  "assembly.option.contigs": "{count, plural, one {# contig} other {# contigs}}",
  "assembly.circularNotReported": "not reported by {assembler}",
  "assembly.columnsNote.spades": "Length and GC are computed by ARVA from the contigs file. Coverage is SPAdes' k-mer coverage, read from each contig's name (NODE_…_cov_…): how many times, on average, each of the contig's k-mers (largest k) occurs in the reads. It is lower than read depth and not comparable with other assemblers' coverage. SPAdes reports neither circularity nor repeats.",
  "assembly.columnsNote.unicycler": "Length and GC are computed by ARVA from the contigs file. Depth and circularity are Unicycler's: depth is relative to the main replicons (about 1.00× for the chromosome), not a read depth; circular means a completed replicon whose end joins its start in the graph. In long-read-only assemblies Unicycler 0.5.0 writes neither in the FASTA, and ARVA reads them from its assembly.gfa.",
  "assembly.columnsNote.imported": "Length and GC are computed by ARVA from the genome FASTA. Coverage and circularity are not known: ARVA did not assemble this genome and reads neither from the FASTA. If the assembler you used reported them (for example Flye's assembly_info.txt), they are in its own output, not in ARVA.",
  "assembly.compare.coverageKinds": "These assemblers report different kinds of coverage (read depth, k-mer coverage, relative depth): compare coverage only between assemblies of the same assembler.",
