  "polishing.medaka.models": "Models in Medaka {version}'s package (checksums checked against conda's record): {models}.",
  "polishing.medaka.fixed": "Always passed: -i, -d, -o, -m and the thread count (-t, used for alignment, inference and stitching; medaka's README notes that inference scales poorly beyond 2 threads and uses about threads + 4). Gap filling from the draft (medaka's default) is kept; --bacteria is not offered (its model is not in the package).",
