  "polishing.heap": "Java heap (GB)",
  "polishing.heapHint": "Pilon's memory (-Xmx), at most {max} GB. Empty: {default} GB (the performance profile's memory per job, raised towards the 8 GB Pilon's documentation gives for a bacterial genome, within what ARVA may give a tool less 1 GB for Java's own overhead and ARVA's other services, at most the 16 GB of Debian's pilon launcher).",
  "polishing.heapBelowDocumented": "Pilon's documentation asks for at least {min} GB for a bacterial genome with ~200x Illumina coverage (16 GB recommended; as a rule of thumb 1 GB per megabase). Here ARVA may give a tool at most {max} GB, and by default keeps 1 GB of it for Java's own overhead and ARVA's other services, so Pilon may run out of memory: give ARVA more memory (with Docker Desktop, in its Resources settings).",
  "polishing.stopWhenUnchanged": "Stop after a round that changes nothing",
