  "import.note.duplicates": "Identical files are rejected as duplicates within a sample; identical content already in another sample of the project is accepted with a note.",
  "tool.description.seqkit": "Ultrafast toolkit for FASTA/FASTQ manipulation; ARVA uses `seqkit stats` as an independent cross-check of its own read statistics.",
  "tool.description.fastqc": "Widely used quality-control report for high-throughput sequencing reads (per-base quality, sequence content, duplication, adapter content…).",
  "tool.description.fastp": "All-in-one FASTQ preprocessor for short reads: quality control, adapter trimming, quality/length filtering and an HTML/JSON report.",
  "tool.description.filtlong": "Filters long reads by length and quality, keeping the best reads; outputs a subset of the input reads (it never edits read sequences unless trimming is requested).",
  "tool.description.multiqc": "Gathers the FastQC, fastp, SeqKit and Filtlong results of a project's samples into one interactive HTML report. It shows the values those tools computed; it measures nothing new.",
  "tool.description.nanoplot": "Summary statistics and an interactive HTML report for long reads (Oxford Nanopore, PacBio): read length and quality distributions, yield by length, and length against quality.",
  "tool.description.flye": "De novo assembler for long reads (Oxford Nanopore, PacBio) based on repeat graphs; writes contigs, the assembly graph and per-contig coverage, circularity and repeat flags.",
  "tool.description.spades": "De Bruijn graph assembler for short reads (Illumina); in isolate mode it assembles bacterial isolates and writes contigs, scaffolds and the assembly graph, each sequence with its k-mer coverage.",
  "tool.description.unicycler": "Assembly pipeline for bacterial isolates: short reads (an optimised SPAdes run), long reads (miniasm and Racon) or both (short-read-first hybrid assembly); circularises and rotates complete replicons.",
  "tool.description.quast": "Quality assessment of genome assemblies: contiguity (N50, L50, contig lengths) for every assembly, and with a reference genome also genome fraction, misassemblies, mismatches and indels; compares several assemblies in one report with Icarus contig viewers.",
  "tool.description.racon": "Consensus polishing of an assembly with long reads (Oxford Nanopore or PacBio) aligned to it; generic, with no model of a technology's errors. Unicycler also uses it.",
  "tool.description.medaka": "Consensus polishing of Oxford Nanopore assemblies (Flye's in particular) with a neural network trained for the reads' basecaller model; ARVA uses the models its package ships.",
  "tool.description.pilon": "Improves an assembly with short-read alignments: corrects bases and small insertions or deletions, fills gaps and fixes local misassemblies, and lists every change.",
  "tool.description.minimap2": "Aligns long reads to an assembly; ARVA uses it for Racon's overlaps and to measure how well the reads agree with an assembly before and after polishing.",
  "tool.description.bwa": "Aligns short reads to an assembly (BWA-MEM); ARVA uses it to give Pilon its alignments and to measure how well the reads agree with an assembly before and after polishing.",
  "tool.description.samtools": "Sorts and indexes read alignments and summarises them (mapped reads, edit distance, depth); Flye also calls it, and ARVA uses it for polishing.",
  "tool.description.dnadiff": "Aligns two assemblies with NUCmer and lists their differences base by base; ARVA uses it as the direct evidence of what polishing changed.",
  "tool.description.bakta": "Annotation of bacterial genomes and plasmids with a versioned database: tRNA, tmRNA, rRNA, ncRNA, CRISPR arrays, CDS and small ORFs with functional annotation by alignment-free identification and protein clusters, pseudogenes (full database), gaps and origins of replication/transfer.",
  "tool.description.prokka": "Annotation of prokaryotic genomes: Prodigal gene calls with similarity search of the proteins, tRNA and tmRNA (Aragorn) and rRNA (barrnap). Its README states that it is no longer maintained by its author, who recommends Bakta; ARVA offers it as an alternative.",
  "tools.subtitle": "External tools ARVA can run. ARVA detects them but never installs anything by itself.",
