  "databases.catalogue.bakta-light.description": "The light Bakta database: all non-coding feature information, but only UniRef50 cluster information (PSCC) for coding sequences, so annotations of proteins are less specific than with the full database. Smaller and faster.",
  "databases.catalogue.bakta-light.note0": "Bakta 1.12.2's AMR expert system reads an AMRFinderPlus database from amrfinderplus-db/latest inside this folder (bakta/expert/amrfinder.py) and needs AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7 or later (bakta/utils.py). The light 6.0 archive contains amrfinderplus-db/2024-12-18.1 (database format 4.0.1) with latest linking to it, the release its version.json lists (seen when ARVA installed it on 2026-10-28; the full archive was not downloaded to check).",
  "databases.catalogue.bakta-light.note1": "Bakta's own installer (bakta_db download) then also runs amrfinder_update --force_update, which fetches an AMRFinderPlus database from NCBI, a version neither Bakta nor ARVA pins. ARVA does not, so the AMRFinderPlus data stay the release this database was built with; updating them would be a separate, recorded step.",
  "databases.catalogue.bakta-full.description": "The full Bakta database, recommended by Bakta for the most specific annotations and all features. It needs tens of gigabytes: about 32 GB to download and 84 GB unpacked.",
  "databases.catalogue.bakta-full.note0": "Bakta 1.12.2's AMR expert system reads an AMRFinderPlus database from amrfinderplus-db/latest inside this folder (bakta/expert/amrfinder.py) and needs AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7 or later (bakta/utils.py). The light 6.0 archive contains amrfinderplus-db/2024-12-18.1 (database format 4.0.1) with latest linking to it, the release its version.json lists (seen when ARVA installed it on 2026-10-28; the full archive was not downloaded to check).",
  "databases.catalogue.bakta-full.note1": "Bakta's own installer (bakta_db download) then also runs amrfinder_update --force_update, which fetches an AMRFinderPlus database from NCBI, a version neither Bakta nor ARVA pins. ARVA does not, so the AMRFinderPlus data stay the release this database was built with; updating them would be a separate, recorded step.",
  "databases.catalogue.amrfinderplus.description": "NCBI's database of antimicrobial resistance genes and point mutations, read by AMRFinderPlus (and by Bakta's AMR expert system). Planned with the AMRFinderPlus integration.",
  "databases.catalogue.checkm2.description": "The protein database CheckM2 uses to estimate genome completeness and contamination. Planned with the genome quality module.",
