  "species.sectionTitle": "Species identification (ANI)",
  "species.intro": "Identify the species of an assembly by average nucleotide identity (ANI) against a reference genome collection you registered (FastANI or skani), or with Mash, sylph or GTDB-Tk when their databases are registered. ARVA names a species only when the evidence supports it, and the result can only be as good as the collection searched.",
  "species.start": "Identify species",
  "species.empty": "No species identification yet",
  "species.emptyHint": "Choose an assembly, a method and a reference collection.",
  "species.title": "Identify the species",
  "species.description": "ARVA compares the assembly with every genome of the chosen database and reads the ranked hits against the 95 % ANI species boundary, showing why a result is ambiguous when it is.",
  "species.assembly": "Assembly",
  "species.assemblyHint": "Any assembly of the sample: a draft or a polished one.",
  "species.method": "Method",
  "species.methodHint": "Each method measures something different; FastANI and skani are validated with ARVA against reference genome collections.",
  "species.methodName.fastani": "FastANI",
  "species.methodName.skani": "skani",
  "species.methodName.mash": "Mash",
  "species.methodName.sylph": "sylph",
  "species.methodName.gtdbtk": "GTDB-Tk",
  "species.methodWhat.fastani": "Fragment-based ANI: the assembly is cut into 3 kb fragments, each mapped to every reference; ANI is the mean identity of the reciprocal mappings, and the aligned fraction is the share of fragments mapped.",
  "species.methodWhat.skani": "Sparse-chaining ANI: approximate alignments of sampled k-mers give the ANI and the aligned fraction of each genome; robust to fragmented assemblies.",
  "species.methodWhat.mash": "MinHash distance against a sketch file (for example RefSeq): a fast screen. The distance estimates a k-mer mutation rate; it is not ANI.",
  "species.methodWhat.sylph": "Containment ANI against a sylph database (for example GTDB), from sampled k-mers. Built for reads; on an assembly ARVA reads its unadjusted ANI.",
  "species.methodWhat.gtdbtk": "Classification in the Genome Taxonomy Database (marker genes, placement in the GTDB tree, ANI to species representatives). Needs about 100 GB of data and about 140 GB of memory.",
  "species.methodRange.fastani": "FastANI reports no ANI for pairs much below 80 % (FastANI README), so a genome without a close reference gives no hit. It reads the references as FASTA files (a reference genome collection).",
  "species.methodRange.skani": "skani screens out pairs below about 80 % identity (-s 80) and reports a pair only when one genome has more than 15 % aligned (--min-af 15); its learned ANI model is on by default.",
  "species.methodRange.mash": "ARVA ranks the sketches by distance and applies no species boundary. Checked with ARVA on a small test database only.",
  "species.methodRange.sylph": "On an assembly sylph cannot correct for coverage (each k-mer is seen about once); ARVA reads Naive_ANI and the containment of each reference. Checked with ARVA on a small test database only.",
  "species.methodRange.gtdbtk": "GTDB-Tk applies the GTDB species radius (usually 95 % ANI) and an aligned fraction of at least 0.5. ARVA does not start it when the performance profile gives a run less memory than GTDB-Tk's documentation requires. Not validated with ARVA.",
  "species.validation.validated": "validated with ARVA",
