  "tool.description.abricate": "Nucleotide BLAST screen of assembled contigs against the databases ABRicate bundles; ARVA uses its VFDB (virulence factors) and PlasmidFinder (plasmid replicons) databases.",
  "tool.description.mobsuite": "Plasmid reconstruction and typing from assembled contigs (mob_recon, with mob_typer on each reconstructed plasmid): each contig's chromosome or plasmid call, replicon and relaxase types, MPF, oriT and predicted mobility, against MOB-suite's plasmid database.",
  "tool.description.integronfinder": "Integrons in assembled contigs: the integron integrase (intI), attC recombination sites, and optionally the Pc promoter and attI site, as complete integrons, In0 (intI without attC) or CALIN (attC sites without intI).",
  "tool.description.isescan": "Insertion sequence elements in assembled contigs, complete and partial, with transposase profile HMMs and terminal inverted repeats.",
  "tool.description.genomad": "Plasmids and viruses (proviruses inside host contigs included) in assembled contigs, from gene markers and a neural network, against geNomad's database.",
  "databases.kind.plasmidfinder.tool1": "no version requirement is stated in the database repository",
  "databases.kind.plasmidfinder.unconfirmed1": "Which plasmidfinder_db commit ABRicate 1.4.0's copy was taken from: its files do not say.",
  "databases.kind.mobsuite.unconfirmed0": "NCBI publishes no checksum for the dated taxonomy archives; ARVA records the SHA-256 of the one it downloaded.",
  "databases.kind.vfdb.tool1": "VFDB's download page states no requirement",
  "databases.kind.vfdb.unconfirmed2": "Which VFDB release ABRicate 1.4.0's copy was taken from: its files do not say.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.name": "NCBI 16S ribosomal RNA (type strains)",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.description": "NCBI's BLAST database of 16S rRNA sequences of Bacteria and Archaea type strains (RefSeq Targeted Loci), for naming the organism of a Sanger 16S read or consensus with blastn.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.recognise": "16S_ribosomal_RNA.nsq, .nin and .nhr with the other files of a version 5 BLAST database (.ndb, .nnd, .nni, .nog, .nos, .not, .ntf, .nto); 16S_ribosomal_RNA-nucl-metadata.json when kept. blastdbcmd -info is read for the title, date, sequence count and BLAST database version.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.version_from": "\"last-updated\" in 16S_ribosomal_RNA-nucl-metadata.json (the build date, e.g. 2026-10-29); without that file, the date blastdbcmd -info prints. NCBI keeps only the current build.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.typical_size": "Build of 2026-10-29: 72,729,050-byte archive; the database files are about 18 MB (27,646 sequences), NCBI's taxonomy files in the same archive about 295 MB more.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.download_note": "NCBI publishes only the current build, as one archive with an MD5 file and a metadata file giving its date. After you confirm the size and date, ARVA downloads it over HTTPS, checks the MD5 and extracts only the database files (NCBI's taxonomy files only if you ask). It never runs update_blastdb.pl. An older build is available only if you kept it: register its folder.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.licence": "NCBI places no restrictions on the use or distribution of the data; some submitters may claim rights in their data (NCBI website and data usage policies)",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.tool0": "BLAST+ 2.12.0 (the version ARVA runs) reads the current build, a version 5 BLAST database (blastdbcmd -info and blastn checked on the 2026-10-29 build)",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.unconfirmed0": "Which citation NCBI asks for this database: the pages read do not say; ARVA cites RefSeq.",
  "databases.kind.ncbi_16s.unconfirmed1": "Whether NCBI keeps older builds anywhere: none is on the FTP listing.",
  "databases.kind.genomad.unconfirmed0": "geNomad and this database were not installed on ARVA's test machine (disk): the integration is written from geNomad 1.13.0's source and not validated with a real run.",
  "databases.catalogue.mobsuite-3.1.8.description": "MOB-suite's reference plasmids (with their MOB-cluster assignments), replicon, relaxase, MPF and oriT sequences and repetitive elements, read by mob_recon and mob_typer. ARVA prepares the folder as mob_init would (BLAST indexes, Mash sketch, NCBI taxonomy) without running mob_init.",
  "databases.catalogue.mobsuite-3.1.8.terms": "Licence of the Zenodo record: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. Cite MOB-suite. The NCBI taxonomy ARVA adds for host-range predictions is NCBI data (public domain).",
  "databases.catalogue.mobsuite-3.1.8.compatibility": "The database mob_init of MOB-suite 3.1.9 downloads (mob_suite/config.json: Zenodo 10304948).",
  "databases.catalogue.mobsuite-3.1.8.extracted": "1,656,164,567 bytes unpacked, of which ncbi_plasmid_full_seqs.fas is 1,641,486,485 (listing of the archive, 2026-10-29); prepared by ARVA without that FASTA, the folder holds 1,413,260,939 bytes (BLAST index, Mash sketch, taxa.sqlite of taxdmp_2026-10-01)",
  "databases.catalogue.mobsuite-3.1.8.note0": "mob_init downloads this archive with TLS verification turned off and then the latest NCBI taxonomy over plain HTTP (ete3); ARVA downloads the archive over HTTPS, compares its MD5 with Zenodo's, and builds taxa.sqlite from the dated NCBI taxonomy archive you confirm.",
  "databases.catalogue.mobsuite-3.1.8.note1": "The reference plasmids' FASTA (1.6 GB) is only searched through its BLAST index by mob_recon 3.1.9; ARVA keeps it only when you ask, and records its SHA-256 either way.",
  "databases.mobsuite.title": "Preparing the MOB-suite database (as mob_init would, without running it)",
